    <node id="COVID-19">
      <data key="d0">COVID-19</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">**COVID-19: A Severe and Contagious Respiratory Disease Caused by the SARS-CoV-2 Virus**

COVID-19 is a severe and contagious respiratory disease caused by the SARS-CoV-2 virus, which has become a global pandemic and poses a significant threat to global health. First identified in Wuhan, China in the fall of 2019, the SARS-CoV-2 virus has spread globally, infecting millions of people and causing widespread illness worldwide.

Characterized by various manifestations, including fever, fatigue, anosmia, ageusia, cough, and nasal congestion, COVID-19 can result in severe health issues, including respiratory problems and death. The disease has been mentioned as the underlying condition of several patients, indicating its severe impact on individuals.

As a viral respiratory illness, COVID-19 requires coordinated health responses and vaccination efforts to contain its spread. The pandemic has resulted in long-term health consequences for some individuals, including respiratory, cardiovascular, and other systemic complications. The virus has originated from Wuhan, Hubei, China and has since spread globally, causing widespread illness and disruption to healthcare systems.

The COVID-19 pandemic is an ongoing global public health emergency caused by the SARS-CoV-2 virus, with significant impact on various populations, including the AIAN population in Arizona. It is essential to acknowledge the far-reaching consequences of this disease, which has become a major public health concern worldwide.

In summary, COVID-19 is a severe and contagious respiratory disease caused by the SARS-CoV-2 virus, characterized by various symptoms, and has resulted in widespread illness and disruption to healthcare systems globally.</data>
