    <node id="SARS-CoV-2">
      <data key="d0">SARS-CoV-2</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">**SARS-CoV-2: A Novel Coronavirus Responsible for the COVID-19 Pandemic**

SARS-CoV-2, also known as the Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome CoronaVirus 2, is a type of virus that causes COVID-19, a respiratory disease that has spread globally. This novel coronavirus was identified as the causative agent behind the COVID-19 pandemic. The virus can cause a range of symptoms, from mild to severe, including no symptoms at all. In some individuals, it may trigger autoimmune diseases and autoimmune manifestations, such as myositis.

The symptoms of COVID-19 can vary in severity, with some individuals experiencing severe respiratory distress. SARS-CoV-2 is a significant public health concern, and efforts to understand and respond to its spread continue to be an urgent priority. The virus is responsible for the COVID-19 disease, which has led to widespread illness and death around the world. It is also known to cause the COVID-19 pandemic, a global outbreak of the disease that has affected millions of people.

The SARS-CoV-2 virus is highly contagious and can spread from person to person through respiratory droplets produced when an infected person coughs or sneezes. The virus can be identified by the presence of nucleocapsid protein antibodies, and it has been the subject of extensive research and study since its identification in December 2019. Efforts to combat the spread of the virus have included the development of vaccines, treatments, and public health measures aimed at reducing transmission and mitigating the disease's impact.

It is worth noting that an isolated case of a person testing negative for SARS-CoV-2 on day 47, as determined by a PCR examination, does not indicate the presence or absence of the virus in general. Overall, SARS-CoV-2 is the causative agent of COVID-19, a viral disease characterized by pneumonia and other respiratory complications.&lt;SEP&gt;SARS-CoV-2 is a viral strain causing COVID-19.&lt;SEP&gt;A species of coronavirus that causes COVID-19.</data>
