    <node id="Patient">
      <data key="d0">Patient</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">**Patient**

The term patient refers to an individual receiving or having received medical care, exhibiting a diverse range of characteristics and scenarios. This encompasses individuals admitted to hospitals for various conditions, such as COVID-19 infections, often complicated by autoimmune manifestations. Patients may experience a wide range of symptoms, including oral lesions, which have been successfully treated in one case with significant improvement after 10 days.

Patients may have complex medical conditions, such as valvulopathy, pericardial effusion, and hemodynamic involvement, requiring multifaceted diagnostic and therapeutic approaches. A patient's medical history, clinical features, and radiological findings must be thoroughly investigated and evaluated to ensure accurate diagnosis and treatment.

Patients may require personalized approaches to diagnosis and care, taking into account their unique medical history, clinical features, and radiological findings. In some instances, patients may be recipients of transplants, such as a 47-year-old male patient undergoing a second cadaver donor kidney transplant evaluation.

Specific scenarios include a hospital patient undergoing treatment and monitoring for a thrombus, a subject with primary immunodeficiency who presented with multiple laboratory results and genetic testing, an individual undergoing a chest x-ray examination to diagnose bronchiectasis, a 35-year-old female patient with a history of COVID-19 vaccination and subsequent development of cerebral venous sinus thrombosis (CVST), a 40-year-old African American female with past medical history of hypertension, tobacco use, and Graves' disease who presented with acute painless left eye vision loss after vaccination, and a patient diagnosed with polycythemia vera, experiencing multiple arterial thromboses and left posterior cerebral artery/posterior inferior cerebellar artery stroke.

In summary, the term patient encompasses a wide range of characteristics, medical conditions, and treatment approaches, necessitating a comprehensive, personalized approach to diagnosis and care.&lt;SEP&gt;A 37-year-old man without any known comorbidity.&lt;SEP&gt;An 11-year-old girl suffering from severe symptoms including fever, vomiting, and abdominal pain.&lt;SEP&gt;The patient was diagnosed with catarrhal appendicitis and underwent treatment with vasoactive drugs.&lt;SEP&gt;The patient was treated for COVID-19 and ARDS before being weaned off HFNO after 9 days.</data>
