    <node id="Table 1">
      <data key="d0">Table 1</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Table 1 is a comprehensive clinical data table that presents a compilation of numerical and descriptive data associated with patient diagnostic results. It is a tabular representation of clinical findings in patients with Multi-System Inflammatory Syndrome in Children (MIS-C) and is used to show the laboratory results of their cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) over the course of hospitalization. The table includes a range of data, such as patient symptoms, biochemistry indicators, and laboratory results, which were gradually returned to normal levels during hospitalization.

The primary function of Table 1 is to present data in an organized and easily accessible format, allowing for quick and accurate decision-making in clinical settings. The table can be used for various purposes, including analyzing and interpreting patient data, tracking the progression of the disease, and evaluating the effectiveness of treatments administered.

Table 1 contains information on the patient's laboratory results, including cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) analysis, biochemistry indicators, and serum hormone levels. It also provides details on the patient's medications and any relevant test results, such as the presence or absence of anti-dsDNA and anti-LKM1 antibodies. The table serves as a critical tool for healthcare professionals to review and analyze the patient's condition, facilitating informed decision-making and enabling them to provide optimal care.

The table's content is based on a comprehensive clinical data analysis, which includes laboratory results, clinical findings, and treatment information. The data presented in Table 1 provides valuable insights into the patient's condition, allowing healthcare professionals to better understand the disease progression and respond accordingly. The table's primary function is to present data in a clear and concise manner, enabling quick and accurate interpretation, which is essential in clinical settings where timely decision-making is crucial.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 1 is a medical diagnostic tool.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical reference table mentioned in the input text.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3b02ad23c5895936b3c0b71851649c2a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8e2b2829047cd45b23c8d541e98ba364-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2bab568fd0945ca97229932b3958ca4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2bab568fd0945ca97229932b3958ca4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4d950b29becfb92828ce9bf62c55083-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f020ad0a2c0ecdec4208d99f1323b71a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f20b43850bf66bd2b3a28373aa471cc9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a6b1da4c7da3290d7d05a67bc6887c2b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-37b86b5550564c8fffdac9d2aa3847fa-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8faeb94ce116f4335d47a4477fb5a990-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8faeb94ce116f4335d47a4477fb5a990-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4301fdd6d220edec2508fe3ab73d329f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-45342268eca0e779888f14d37fa7cfca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-45342268eca0e779888f14d37fa7cfca-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4389b6cb92af87d5a04e2441adde5d99-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-08b0574b124b4b202cf913a692661565-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-08b0574b124b4b202cf913a692661565-chunk-002</data>
