    <node id="C-reactive protein">
      <data key="d0">C-reactive protein</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">C-reactive protein (CRP) is a protein present in the blood that indicates inflammation. It is a blood test used to measure levels of inflammation in the body. This protein increases in response to inflammation, indicating the presence of an underlying condition such as infection or disease.

The levels of CRP in the blood are often elevated during inflammatory or infectious processes. A laboratory test is used to measure CRP, which helps healthcare professionals diagnose and monitor various conditions, including infections, autoimmune diseases, and cancers. The results of this test are crucial in determining the severity of inflammation and guiding treatment decisions.

It is essential to note that while CRP is a valuable tool for assessing inflammation, it is not exclusive to this condition. The test results must be interpreted in conjunction with other clinical findings and diagnostic tests to provide a comprehensive understanding of the underlying condition.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-cd00db0ae9ecbe44b58bb940c8d22e91-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8e2b2829047cd45b23c8d541e98ba364-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2bab568fd0945ca97229932b3958ca4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-397d75bf96c654d226460be3bdf675fd-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b74fd1be0bac20260caf978512133533-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7eb60a9a94338d8cb72e8be2c77c851d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f41dbcd0ad3671a2ac5da13460b3f44-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6f41dbcd0ad3671a2ac5da13460b3f44-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5bdb1a3963218454e869ba51d8709816-chunk-000</data>
