    <node id="Chest X-ray">
      <data key="d0">Chest X-ray</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">**Chest X-ray**

A chest X-ray is a medical imaging test used to visualize internal structures of the chest cavity. It is a diagnostic imaging technique that involves using X-rays to produce images of the lungs and chest cavity. This non-invasive imaging technique is often used for the detection of abnormalities such as pleural effusion, cardiomegaly, and prominent bronchovascular markings. Chest X-rays are typically used to produce images of the chest region, which can be particularly useful in confirming the progression of lung disease, as in the case where the test was used to confirm the progression of lung disease in an individual. Additionally, chest X-rays can be used to visualize internal structures of the body, providing images of the chest cavity. In certain instances, chest X-rays have revealed abnormalities such as large left-sided pneumothorax, which requires immediate medical attention. Overall, chest X-rays are an essential diagnostic tool for medical professionals in assessing and diagnosing chest-related conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-6a5889e2c77746885a05d3aeb6ed5e4a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8e2b2829047cd45b23c8d541e98ba364-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bd19502a29f3f6f294b8182dbd43e0b9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4d950b29becfb92828ce9bf62c55083-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4d950b29becfb92828ce9bf62c55083-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9e2af8011ab47c55dd96b1f453c4d299-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aa260e9207bb6144bb25f98ed8b77838-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-397d75bf96c654d226460be3bdf675fd-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b11d21ed4c1de5a364f9078d6a43e651-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b11d21ed4c1de5a364f9078d6a43e651-chunk-001</data>
