    <node id="MIS-C">
      <data key="d0">MIS-C</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">MIS-C, or Multisystem Inflammatory Syndrome in children, is a rare but severe inflammatory condition associated with COVID-19 in children. This condition is characterized by fever, rash, and multi-organ involvement. It is a complication of COVID-19 infection, resulting from an abnormal immune response to the SARS-CoV-2 virus. The symptoms of MIS-C can vary, but typically include a range of systemic inflammation and can affect various body parts including the cardiovascular, renal, and respiratory systems.

MIS-C is often distinguished by its lack of respiratory symptoms, unlike COVID-19. The causes of MIS-C are not fully understood, but it is believed to result from an excessive and uncontrolled immune response to the SARS-CoV-2 virus, leading to the development of inflammatory processes within the body. While COVID-19 primarily affects respiratory health, MIS-C represents a more severe and widespread impact on the body's systems.

Multiple cases of MIS-C have been reported worldwide, often in children under the age of 16, although the condition can also affect older individuals. Early recognition and treatment of MIS-C are crucial, as it requires prompt medical care to manage and hopefully resolve the condition before serious complications arise.

In summary, MIS-C is a rare but serious condition associated with COVID-19 in children and young individuals, resulting from an overactive immune response to the SARS-CoV-2 virus.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-c2bab568fd0945ca97229932b3958ca4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2bab568fd0945ca97229932b3958ca4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2bab568fd0945ca97229932b3958ca4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-397d75bf96c654d226460be3bdf675fd-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b74fd1be0bac20260caf978512133533-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-08b0574b124b4b202cf913a692661565-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-08b0574b124b4b202cf913a692661565-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-08b0574b124b4b202cf913a692661565-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1790411631</data>
