    <node id="Rituximab">
      <data key="d0">Rituximab</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Rituximab is a monoclonal antibody medication primarily used in the treatment of various autoimmune diseases. As an immunosuppressive drug, it is employed to suppress the immune system's abnormal activity, thereby alleviating symptoms associated with autoimmune disorders.

Rituximab's therapeutic applications extend to the treatment of pemphigus vulgaris, a condition characterized by blistering of the skin. Additionally, this medication has been used in immunotherapy, a medical approach that involves modifying or stimulating the immune system to treat or prevent disease.

The medication works by targeting specific cells in the immune system, eliminating any abnormalities that may be causing the autoimmune disease. Rituximab's efficacy makes it an invaluable treatment option for patients suffering from autoimmune-related disorders, including B-cell related cancers.

It's essential to note that Rituximab is often administered through an antibody infusion, providing targeted treatment to affected areas of the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-936f3c0323bd4447ee7bbc89993bf6ea-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9830f31d51c915a5d63cd25e5ee2876c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e6fac4d0ace145ccea7831fee370c35-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e6fac4d0ace145ccea7831fee370c35-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e3f3c4d8f66d7495a702536a1895bbb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e3f3c4d8f66d7495a702536a1895bbb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4cac2addca2717d86125cd3a997e5bd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8796f4ace49bbe8576f6ef1d7428f138-chunk-001</data>
