    <node id="hydatid disease">
      <data key="d0">hydatid disease</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A parasitic infection caused by the Echinococcus tapeworm, resulting in the formation of cysts in organs such as the liver, lungs, and brain.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical condition involving a parasitic infection that affects the body's tissues and organs, characterized by the formation of cysts and the presence of viable protoscolices.&lt;SEP&gt;A parasitic infection caused by the larvae of the tapeworm Echinococcus granulosus, characterized by the formation of cysts in various organs, including the liver, lungs, and brain. Symptoms include fever, abdominal pain, and weight loss.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-b11d21ed4c1de5a364f9078d6a43e651-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-03b0a8dfeb808417cea94ea14849fbdf-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-03b0a8dfeb808417cea94ea14849fbdf-chunk-002</data>
