    <edge source="COVID-19" target="Patient">
      <data key="d7">10.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The COVID-19 Patient

The COVID-19 patient in question was infected with the virus, which is now regarded as a global pandemic. The patient's symptoms, which manifested a month prior to the current illness, suggest that COVID-19 is the primary cause of the exacerbation of Immune thrombocytopenic purpura (ITP). As it is a severe respiratory illness, the patient's case necessitated hospitalization due to complications from COVID-19.

Notably, however, the patient and their brother were exposed to COVID-19, which suggests they contracted it outside of a hospital setting. As an infectious disease caused by the virus SARS-CoV-2, COVID-19 has become a public health issue worldwide. This patient's experience with COVID-19 is illustrative of the virus's effects on patients, especially those with compromised immune systems.

The COVID-19 patient was also affected by systemic complications arising from the administration of Sinopharm vaccine followed by Neotigason 25 mg/D and other short-term therapeutic interventions intended to address the exacerbation of generalized pustular psoriasis.&lt;SEP&gt;the patient was tested negative for COVID-19.&lt;SEP&gt;Was diagnosed with COVID-19.</data>
